.TH TPAC 1 "2026" "titanpkg 0.1.0" "ArchTitan OS Manual"
.SH NAME
tpac, titanpkg \- standalone package manager for ArchTitan OS subsystems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tpac
.RI [ options ]
.B \-Syu
.RI [ package ...]
.br
.B tpac
.RI [ options ]
.B \-S
.I package ...
.br
.B tpac
.RI [ options ]
.B \-Rns
.I package ...
.br
.B tpac
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tpac
(\fBtitanpkg\fR)
installs, upgrades, verifies and rolls back first-party ArchTitan OS subsystem
packages (\fItitan-hwm\fR, \fItitan-ui\fR, \fItitan-sysmon\fR,
\fItitan-quicksettings\fR, \fIarchtitan-guard\fR, etc.) alongside \fBpacman\fR(8)
without modifying \fI/var/lib/pacman\fR or overwriting pacman-owned files.
.SH PACMAN-STYLE OPERATIONS
.TP
.B \-Syu \fR[\fIpkg\fR...]
Synchronize repository databases and upgrade all installed Titan subsystems.
.TP
.B \-S \fIpkg\fR...
Install (or reinstall, unless \fB\-\-needed\fR is given) one or more packages.
.TP
.B \-Sy
Refresh repository index databases only.
.TP
.B \-Su \fR[\fIpkg\fR...]
Upgrade installed packages without refreshing repository indexes.
.TP
.B \-Ss \fIquery\fR
Search package names and descriptions across enabled repositories.
.TP
.B \-Si \fIpkg\fR, \fB\-Qi \fIpkg\fR
Display package metadata, dependencies and available versions.
.TP
.B \-Sl
List all available packages in enabled repositories.
.TP
.B \-Sc\fR, \fB\-Scc
Prune old cached package archives (\fB\-Sc\fR) or remove all cached packages
and repository indexes (\fB\-Scc\fR).
.TP
.B \-R \fIpkg\fR..., \fB\-Rs \fIpkg\fR..., \fB\-Rns \fIpkg\fR...
Remove installed packages. With \fB\-s\fR, also remove orphaned dependencies.
With \fB\-n\fR, skip saving modified configuration files as \fI.pacsave\fR.
.TP
.B \-Q
List installed Titan packages and versions.
.TP
.B \-Qu
List installed Titan packages with newer versions available.
.TP
.B \-Ql \fIpkg\fR
List all files owned by an installed package.
.TP
.B \-Qo \fIpath\fR
Query which installed Titan package owns \fIpath\fR.
.TP
.B \-Qk \fR[\fIpkg\fR...]
Verify installed files on disk against recorded SHA-256 digests and modes.
.TP
.B \-Qdt
List orphaned packages installed as dependencies.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
\fBupdate\fR, \fBupgrade\fR, \fBinstall\fR, \fBreinstall\fR, \fBremove\fR,
\fBautoremove\fR, \fBlist\fR, \fBsearch\fR, \fBinfo\fR, \fBfiles\fR, \fBowns\fR,
\fBverify\fR, \fBrollback\fR, \fBclean\fR, \fBdoctor\fR, \fBkey\fR, \fBself-check\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Generic failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage or configuration error.
.TP
.B 3
Dependency or conflict resolution failure.
.TP
.B 4
Security violation (signature, SHA-256, path escape, or ownership failure).
.TP
.B 5
Transaction failure (automatically rolled back).

